<p>Its correct form should be:</p>

<div class="language-sh highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><table class="rouge-table"><tbody><tr><td class="rouge-gutter gl"><pre class="lineno">1
</pre></td><td class="rouge-code"><pre>SQL: UPDATE msg_10003600 SET <span class="nv">chatMsgHeight</span><span class="o">=</span>? WHERE <span class="o">((</span><span class="nv">messageId</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s1">'936542df77de41778139a42b4f4be296'</span><span class="o">)</span> AND <span class="o">(</span><span class="nb">type</span><span class="o">=</span>2<span class="o">))</span>
</pre></td></tr></tbody></table></code></pre></div></div>

<p>No need to think twice — the condition after <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">where</code> in the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">SQL</code> statement was always <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">true</code>, which produced this bug so elementary it couldn’t get any more elementary.</p>

<p>Here’s the corrected code:</p>

<div class="language-objc highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><table class="rouge-table"><tbody><tr><td class="rouge-gutter gl"><pre class="lineno">1
